[Music]  economists Wall Street traders and the  president regularly talk about this  america's gross domestic product as you  can see it generally rises over time but  right now the President and some others  say it's not rising fast enough  they say the country will be better off  if we can make the GDP rise at a 3% rate  or even more a year rather than the 2  percent rate it had been going at for a  while will explain why they say the  current rate isn't fast enough but first  you have to understand what GDP is and  how government statisticians measure it  to put it simply GDP is a measure of how  much stuff a nation produces with all of  the work that it does all of the apples  we pick from orchards the cars we  produce in factories the dinners we  serve at restaurants the flights we take  from airports the broken legs our  doctors fix in hospitals and more GDP is  what all of that work adds up to as a  nation we produce an enormous amount of  stuff every single year according to the  Commerce Department Americans produce  nearly 21 trillion dollars worth of  goods and services last year far more  than any other nation including China 21  trillion dollars let's put that big  number in perspective if all we did as a  nation was make cars that would be about  enough car production to build two giant  stacks of car towers to the moon in a  single year so how does the government  measure all that stuff to come up with  GDP the government's method is kind of  odd if it's a measure of how much stuff  we produce as a nation you might think  that government statisticians went  around counting all that production up  but that's not the way the government  does it instead what the government  measures is everything that we consume  the thinking goes like this  what is consumed has to be produced by  somebody somewhere if you measure  consumption you can figure out  production so here's how statisticians  calculate consumption first they can up  everything that's spent by consumers  that's the stuff you buy from day to day  then they add it to everything that's  spent by businesses on investment  that's the stuff businesses buy to grow  and make what you're producing and then  they add that to everything that's spent  by the government on space travel  housing the military and everything else  all together that equals their broad  measure of everything we consume as a  nation the formula is C plus I plus G  then the statisticians make some  adjustments sometimes we make goods or  provide services that get sent overseas  for example America exports a lot of  soybeans that counts toward production  too so we add that to the mix sometimes  we also consume products that we've  imported think about your iphones and  televisions imported from china that's  the stuff we consume that wasn't made  here in america subtract that from the  mix now there's two other adjustments to  make sometimes we consume stuff that was  made earlier and placed in a warehouse  or stuck on the shelf of a store think  about a blouse that was placed in  inventory months ago that somebody buys  today that's something we might consume  today that was produced before to adjust  for these timing changes the  statisticians correct for changes in  inventories they also correct for  inflation prices of stuff tend to go up  over time and statisticians adjust for  those changes taken altogether you get  GDP so what's going on now President  Trump is worried that GDP isn't growing  fast enough between 1950 and 2000 GDP  grew by 3.7 percent per year that means  if we produced 1,000 cars in 1 year we  produced 1037 the next year and 1075 the  year after that since 2000 GDP has grown  by 2 percent a year that would mean 1020  cars in the second year and 1040 in the  year after that changes in the growth  rate can really add up over time at a  three point seven percent growth rate  GDP doubles in 20 years at a 2 percent  growth rate it takes 35 years to double  that's a long time to wait for more  growth  slower GDP growth means slower growth  and family incomes business profits  wealth and prosperity too that's why the  President and others worry when GDP  doesn't grow fast so how can we make it  grow faster remember GDP is a measure of  how much our workers produce two ways to  make GDP grow faster or to add more  workers to the labor force or to  increase the productivity of the ones  we've already got would that make us  better off as a nation well it would  probably help a lot but GDP isn't  everything  it doesn't tell you how the income and  economy produces is distributed between  rich and poor it doesn't tell you  whether your air and water are clean and  it also doesn't tell you whether people  are happy producing all that stuff  that's why we need to look at a lot more  than GDP to know if we're getting better  off as a nation

